Section 301 of the Budget Act, codified as amended at 2 U.S.C. §632. The Budget Act requires that the budget resolution cover the budget year and at least the subsequent four fiscal years. In current practice, it has been common for the budget resolution to cover 10 total fiscal years (the budget year and the subsequent nine fiscal years).

Adoption of the same budget resolution by both chambers is required to trigger enforcement and reconciliation procedures under the Budget Act.

